│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ smooth_biased_path                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite keeps the same interface and return type, but replaces the trivial           │
│                          │ straight-line interpolation with a smooth heuristic trajectory generator tailored to the  │
│                          │ three objectives:                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Minimize distance by starting from the straight line baseline.                         │
│                          │ 2. Reduce school-noise proximity by adding a smooth repulsive bend away from the school   │
│                          │ location.                                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Reduce base-station signal drop by adding a smooth attractive bend toward the base     │
│                          │ location.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation uses only lightweight deterministic math, so it is fast and stable.    │
│                          │ Internally it:                                                                            │
│                          │ - samples uniformly in X exactly as required,                                             │
│                          │ - builds the baseline straight-line Y values,                                             │
│                          │ - applies a Gaussian-shaped repulsion centered near the school X,                         │
│                          │ - applies a broader Gaussian attraction centered near the base X,                         │
│                          │ - limits the total deformation to remain smooth and avoid overly long detours.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This produces a continuous, low-curvature path that typically bends downward when the     │
│                          │ school is above the route and the base is below it, matching the guidance to bend away    │
│                          │ from (40, 20) and toward (70, -30), while still generalizing to other inputs.             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
