│ patch_name               │ anchor_spline_search                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign shifts the program from a single-pass potential-field formula to a small    │
│                          │ planning pipeline:                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Build a geometric context from the inputs.                                             │
│                          │ 2. Generate smooth path candidates from anchor points instead of directly perturbing each │
│                          │ sampled point.                                                                            │
│                          │ 3. Use a monotonic Catmull-Rom style spline over X to create a naturally curved path.     │
│                          │ 4. Run a lightweight internal surrogate search over a few avoidance/attraction parameter  │
│                          │ combinations and select the best candidate.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This structure improves maintainability by separating geometry, candidate generation,     │
│                          │ interpolation, smoothing, and scoring. It also improves performance by producing smoother │
│                          │ globally coordinated curves that bend away from the school region and dip toward the base │
│                          │ station region, rather than relying only on local pointwise forces.                       │
