│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ guided_smooth_multiobjective_path                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the current heuristic with a two-stage “guide + relaxation” strategy that better  │
│                          │ balances all three objectives:                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1) Build a guide curve from the straight line, then:                                      │
│                          │ - push away from school in its X-neighborhood (noise reduction),                          │
│                          │ - pull toward base in its X-neighborhood and mildly in late trajectory (signal            │
│                          │ improvement).                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2) Run iterative Laplacian relaxation with guide anchoring:                               │
│                          │ - reduces local curvature and excess distance,                                            │
│                          │ - preserves smooth continuous bending behavior,                                           │
│                          │ - keeps the trajectory near the multi-objective guide.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This tends to keep F1 controlled while further improving F3, accepting only limited F2    │
│                          │ tradeoff. It also naturally creates a smooth path that bends away from school-like points │
│                          │ (e.g., around (40, 20)) and toward base-like points (e.g., around (70, -30)).             │
