│ patch_name               │ modifier_pipeline_path_generator                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Redesigned the program using an Object-Oriented modifier pipeline architecture. Instead   │
│                          │ of returning a simple straight line, the path is generated by passing each point through  │
│                          │ a series of `PathModifier` objects. A `SchoolAvoidanceModifier` applies a                 │
│                          │ Gaussian-weighted push away from the school, and a `BaseAttractionModifier` applies a     │
│                          │ proportional pull towards the base station. Finally, a cubic window function ensures the  │
│                          │ path remains smoothly anchored to the start and end points while allowing maximum         │
│                          │ deviation in the middle. This structural change makes the path generation highly modular, │
│                          │ easy to tune, and effectively minimizes the multi-objective cost function by balancing    │
│                          │ the three metrics.                                                                        │
