                        Patch Metadata - Gen 11/50 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/10                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ smooth_repulse_attract_path                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach has effectively no optimizer: it uses a pure straight-line           │
│                          │ interpolation with fixed slope, so its implicit parameters are just the linear step size  │
│                          │ `dy` and `num_points`. That keeps F1 very low, but it ignores the two harder objectives:  │
│                          │ avoiding the school region and moving closer to the base station.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new method replaces the trivial line with a smooth parametric multi-objective         │
│                          │ heuristic plus a small deterministic parameter search.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key components and parameters in the new approach:                                        │
│                          │ - **Baseline path**: still starts from the straight line, preserving good F1 behavior.    │
│                          │ - **School repulsion term**:                                                              │
│                          │   - `w_school`: amplitude of the bend away from the school.                               │
│                          │   - `sigma_school`: spatial width of the repulsion bump.                                  │
│                          │   - Direction is chosen adaptively from the relative position of the school to the        │
│                          │ baseline.                                                                                 │
│                          │ - **Base attraction term**:                                                               │
│                          │   - `w_base`: amplitude of the bend toward the base station.                              │
│                          │   - `sigma_base`: spatial width of the attraction bump.                                   │
│                          │   - Direction is also chosen adaptively from the base location relative to the baseline.  │
│                          │ - **Right-side ramp factor**:                                                             │
│                          │   - `ramp_power`: increases attraction influence more strongly near the base-side of the  │
│                          │ route, helping F3 without distorting the early path too much.                             │
│                          │ - **Smoothing**:                                                                          │
│                          │   - `smooth_steps` and `smooth_alpha`: repeated Laplacian smoothing to ensure the         │
│                          │ returned Y-coordinates form a smooth curve instead of a kinked polyline.                  │
│                          │ - **Selection criterion**:                                                                │
│                          │   - A deterministic grid search over candidate parameter settings evaluates a surrogate   │
│                          │ score combining:                                                                          │
│                          │     - approximate path length,                                                            │
│                          │     - school proximity penalty,                                                           │
│                          │     - base distance penalty,                                                              │
│                          │     - curvature penalty.                                                                  │
│                          │   - Lower surrogate score is selected.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this should perform better:                                                           │
│                          │ - It preserves the straight line’s good distance property as a base solution.             │
│                          │ - It explicitly bends **away from (40, 20)** to reduce school-noise proximity.            │
│                          │ - It bends **toward (70, -30)** to reduce signal-loss-related base distance.              │
│                          │ - The parameter search allows different environments to pick a better trade-off than a    │
│                          │ single hard-coded curve.                                                                  │
