│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ sinusoidal_arch_path                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ To minimize the combined score (F1 * F2 * F3), we replace the straight-line path with a   │
│                          │ sinusoidal arch. This arch is designed to bend away from the school located at (40, 20)   │
│                          │ and pass extremely close to the base station at (70, -30). Since the school is at a       │
│                          │ positive Y-coordinate and the base station is at a negative Y-coordinate, a downward arch │
│                          │ simultaneously decreases the school noise proximity (F2) and the base station signal drop │
│                          │ (F3). An amplitude of 37.1 is used to ensure the path passes almost exactly through y =   │
│                          │ -30 when x = 70 (progress = 0.7), which significantly reduces F3 while maintaining a      │
│                          │ reasonable path length (F1).                                                              │
