│ patch_description        │ Add a mild base-focused correction pass after the smoothing rounds. Smoothing tends to    │
│                          │ pull the path away from the base station (which was carefully targeted in the first       │
│                          │ pass), increasing the signal loss (F3). By applying a lightweight update `y +=            │
│                          │ post_base_pull * gaussian(x around bx) * (by - y)` with a small coefficient, the path     │
│                          │ regains some base alignment lost during smoothing, shaving down F3 without materially     │
│                          │ increasing the flying distance (F1).                                                      │
