│ patch_description        │ This rewrite performs a crossover between the simple smooth Gaussian bending idea and the │
│                          │ stronger deterministic candidate-selection idea.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Why this version should score better:                                                     │
│                          │ - It keeps the shortest-path baseline as the foundation for good F1.                      │
│                          │ - It adds a localized smooth repulsion around the school to reduce F2.                    │
│                          │ - It adds a broader attraction around the base station plus a progressive end-of-route    │
│                          │ pull to improve F3 more aggressively.                                                     │
│                          │ - It evaluates a small deterministic grid of candidate trajectories with a lightweight    │
│                          │ surrogate objective, avoiding expensive randomness while preserving efficiency.           │
│                          │ - It applies a mild smoothing pass so the final polyline stays continuous and naturally   │
│                          │ bends away from the school region and toward the base region.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is designed to produce a smooth downward bend in typical benchmark layouts such as   │
│                          │ bending away from `(40, 20)` and toward `(70, -30)`, while remaining robust for general   │
│                          │ inputs.                                                                                   │
