│ patch_name               │ geometry_aware_amplitude                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Make the initial perturbation amplitudes dynamic and geometry-aware. For the school, we   │
│                          │ scale the Gaussian bump amplitude based on the baseline's vertical distance to the school │
│                          │ (`dist_school_y`), maintaining strong localized avoidance when necessary but eliminating  │
│                          │ unnecessary detours when the baseline is safely distant. For the base station, the fixed  │
│                          │ amplitude of 14.0 had a bug: if the baseline passed very close to the base station, this  │
│                          │ fixed bump could cause the path to overshoot and unnecessarily deflect away from the      │
│                          │ target. We cap the attraction bump amplitude relative to the raw vertical distance        │
│                          │ (`dist_base_y * 0.85`), preventing overshooting while allowing a stronger initial guess   │
│                          │ (up to 25.0) when the baseline is far away.                                               │
