│ patch_name               │ dynamic_base_variance_and_sequential_update                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This edit implements the recommendation to use an asymmetric and dynamic Gaussian width   │
│                          │ for the base station attraction. By calculating the X-axis separation between the school  │
│                          │ and the base station, we dynamically adjust the variance of the base station's attraction │
│                          │ field (`base_var`). When the school and base are far apart, a wider base field is used to │
│                          │ maximize signal strength (F3). When they are close, a narrower field is used to prevent   │
│                          │ the base attraction from overriding the school noise repulsion (F2).                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additionally, we revert to the sequential Y-coordinate update (applying school repulsion  │
│                          │ first, then base attraction on the deflected path) and remove the sinusoidal envelope,    │
│                          │ which previously suppressed necessary deformations near the start and end points in the   │
│                          │ best-performing prior program.                                                            │
