│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ school_aware_base_pull                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Introduce a school-aware base-attraction mechanism and relax endpoint suppression so the  │
│                          │ path can recover signal quality more effectively after avoiding the school.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. **Condition base pull on school influence at the same x**: when school repulsion is    │
│                          │ strong, soften base pull to preserve safe deviation; when school influence fades,         │
│                          │ restore/boost pull toward the base to improve F3.                                         │
│                          │ 2. **Reduce over-damping from the current window**: the old cubic window nearly cancels   │
│                          │ shaping near both ends, which can prevent useful late-stage pull toward the base region.  │
│                          │ A floored smooth window keeps paths stable while allowing optimization to act across the  │
│                          │ whole segment.                                                                            │
│                          │ 3. **Retune modifier strengths**: slightly stronger, narrower school repulsion plus       │
│                          │ stronger/wider base attraction tends to preserve F2 while reducing F3 without excessive   │
│                          │ F1 inflation.                                                                             │
