│ patch_description        │ This novel approach abandons the heuristic potential field used in previous iterations    │
│                          │ and instead formulates the path finding as a 1D Dynamic Programming (DP) problem. By      │
│                          │ discretizing the Y-axis into a grid, we can find the globally optimal path that minimizes │
│                          │ a proxy cost function. The cost function is a linear combination of path length (F1),     │
│                          │ school noise (F2), and base signal loss (F3), with weights mathematically derived from    │
│                          │ the local gradients of the multiplier score. This allows the algorithm to make large,     │
│                          │ optimal detours (e.g., aggressively approaching the base) that local heuristics might     │
│                          │ miss, while strictly preventing loops and ensuring smooth progression from start to end.  │
│                          │ A final Laplacian smoothing step removes any grid discretization artifacts.               │
