                        Patch Metadata - Gen 19/50 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/10                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ piecewise_rbf_schedule                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The previous sinusoidal arc hardcoded a bend that completely ignored randomized school    │
│                          │ and base coordinates across different geometry scenarios, unintentionally penalizing the  │
│                          │ base station signal drop metric (F3) by moving to regions with higher line-of-sight loss  │
│                          │ when the base wasn't precisely at the anticipated coordinates.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This implementation replaces the fixed arc with a **Sequential Adaptive Radial Basis      │
│                          │ Function (RBF)** strategy. It establishes a multi-stage deflection algorithm:             │
│                          │ 1. **Base Approaching:** A wider, attractive Gaussian kernel pulls the drone functionally │
│                          │ towards the base station `(y_base)`. The amplitude and standard deviation (`sigma_base`)  │
│                          │ of this pull adapt based on the relative X-axis separation of the base and school.        │
│                          │ 2. **School Avoidance:** Overlapping the base approaching stage, we construct a           │
│                          │ sequential dynamic `school_clearance` logic. Since pulling towards a base could           │
│                          │ inadvertently drag the drone too close to the school, we compute the required Y-clearance │
│                          │ *after* testing the base-pull trajectory. A narrower repulsion kernel corrects the path   │
│                          │ out of the interference zone.                                                             │
│                          │ 3. **Endpoint Ramping:** To prevent huge gradient explosions (Distance penalty F1 jumps)  │
│                          │ near the stationary `start` and `end` points, a seamless linear edge ramp limits all      │
│                          │ lateral RBF deflections from starting with massive Y jumps, allowing mathematically       │
│                          │ continuous trajectories.                                                                  │
