│ patch_name               │ add_post_recovery_pull_and_tune_surrogate                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add a small, localized post-recovery pull near the base station. By applying an           │
│                          │ additional, narrow Gaussian attraction directly towards `by` after the main delta         │
│                          │ calculation, we can specifically trim signal loss (F3) near the base without affecting    │
│                          │ the overall trajectory too much.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Simultaneously, the last iteration drastically increased the baseline amplitude search    │
│                          │ limits, which caused the code to over-optimize F3 at extreme cost to F1 (distance penalty │
│                          │ increased from 1.17 to 1.24). We correct this by strongly increasing the penalty weight   │
│                          │ for `f1` in the `surrogate_score` function to gently force the parameter search back to   │
│                          │ shorter, more optimal geometries.                                                         │
