│ patch_name               │ energy_relax_path                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ I moved away from the previous “compose a few Gaussian offsets + brute-force parameter    │
│                          │ pick” pattern and implemented a **discrete energy minimization** solver.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Inspired by prior programs’ useful intuitions (local school repulsion, base attraction,   │
│                          │ smoothness), this version treats the internal Y points as optimization variables and      │
│                          │ iteratively relaxes them via gradient descent on a multi-objective energy:                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - short path length (F1 proxy),                                                           │
│                          │ - school proximity penalty (F2 proxy),                                                    │
│                          │ - base distance penalty (F3 proxy),                                                       │
│                          │ - curvature regularization and baseline anchoring for smooth, efficient trajectories.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A key design insight is preserved from the feedback: **base attraction is conditioned by  │
│                          │ school influence** (`base_scale = 0.35 + 0.65*(1-w_school)`), so the path keeps the local │
│                          │ school-avoidance bend near the school while recovering toward the base elsewhere.         │
│                          │ This gives a smoother “bend away from (40,20), then bend toward (70,-30)” behavior        │
│                          │ without over-deforming the whole path.                                                    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
