│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ guided_dp_crossover                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This version crosses the strong dynamic-programming path search with the smoother         │
│                          │ guide-curve heuristic.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Argumentation:                                                                            │
│                          │ - The best prior score came from the DP/grid formulation, so that remains the core        │
│                          │ optimizer.                                                                                │
│                          │ - The weaker heuristic still had a useful idea: build a smooth guided curve that bends    │
│                          │ away from the school and toward the base. I use that guide to define a tighter,           │
│                          │ higher-resolution search band instead of a coarse global Y-grid.                          │
│                          │ - The DP objective approximates the three goals directly: short segments for F1,          │
│                          │ inverse-distance penalty near the school for F2, and distance-to-base penalty for F3.     │
│                          │ - After DP, a light anchored smoothing pass reduces grid artifacts without drifting too   │
│                          │ far from the optimized path, then a small final base-attraction correction improves       │
│                          │ signal behavior.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the same input/output behavior, preserves the required markers, and should be  │
│                          │ more efficient and better aligned with the multi-objective score.                         │
