│ patch_name               │ split_kernels_and_rebalance_weights                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This edit implements the recommendation to split the school and base station x-kernels    │
│                          │ more aggressively. Specifically, it narrows the school kernel (`sig_school`) to provide   │
│                          │ sharp local avoidance and broadens the base station kernel (`sig_base`) to provide a more │
│                          │ consistent pull towards the signal source. Additionally, it rebalances the energy         │
│                          │ function weights by increasing the base station attraction (`w_base`) and school          │
│                          │ repulsion (`w_school`) while reducing the path length penalty (`w_len`) and smoothing     │
│                          │ constraint (`w_smooth`). This allows the path to bend more effectively towards the base   │
│                          │ station (reducing F3) while maintaining safety near the school (reducing F2). The number  │
│                          │ of iterations and the learning rate decay are also adjusted to ensure better convergence. │
