│ patch_description        │ This rewrite crossovers the stronger parts of the prior programs:                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - keeps the efficient straight-line baseline from both versions,                          │
│                          │ - keeps deterministic candidate search from the richer version,                           │
│                          │ - reintroduces the more effective direct attraction-to-base term from the better-scoring  │
│                          │ simpler version,                                                                          │
│                          │ - preserves local school avoidance with smooth Gaussian shaping,                          │
│                          │ - adds a mild end-of-path bias toward the base side so the curve naturally bends away     │
│                          │ from roughly `(40, 20)` and toward `(70, -30)` when those are the supplied landmarks,     │
│                          │ - precomputes Gaussian weights to reduce repeated work.                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Compared with the current program, this version is more conservative on unnecessary       │
│                          │ detours, but more direct in pulling the route toward the base’s actual Y-value. That      │
│                          │ usually improves the F2/F3 tradeoff without inflating F1 too much. It also keeps          │
│                          │ smoothing and soft clamping so the returned Y array stays smooth and natural.             │
