│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ smooth_biased_gaussian_path                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite performs a practical crossover of the two implementations:                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - It keeps the stronger parts of the current program:                                     │
│                          │   - adaptive local school avoidance using a clearance concept                             │
│                          │   - endpoint tapering so the path stays smooth and does not over-bend near boundaries     │
│                          │ - It borrows the best structural ideas from the inspiration program:                      │
│                          │   - staged Gaussian shaping                                                               │
│                          │   - a lightweight endpoint-aware smoothing pass                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The main improvement is a more coherent directional strategy: instead of deciding school  │
│                          │ avoidance only from the local intermediate point, the path uses a preferred bend          │
│                          │ direction inferred from the geometry, especially from the base relative to the school.    │
│                          │ This encourages a smooth line that bends away from the school region and then gets pulled │
│                          │ toward the base region, matching the desired behavior of bending away from (40, 20) and   │
│                          │ toward (70, -30).                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Implementation details:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Build the interior X positions and linear baseline.                                     │
│                          │ - Use a smooth edge ramp to suppress unnecessary deformation near start/end.              │
│                          │ - Apply school repulsion first, with dynamic amplitude based on how close the current     │
│                          │ path is to the school Y level.                                                            │
│                          │ - Apply two-stage base attraction:                                                        │
│                          │   - a broad pull for global shaping                                                       │
│                          │   - a narrow pull for local refinement near the base                                      │
│                          │ - Finish with endpoint-aware smoothing to reduce path length inflation while preserving   │
│                          │ the bend.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This remains deterministic, efficient, numerically safe, and preserves the same           │
│                          │ input/output contract.                                                                    │
