│ patch_name               │ quadrature_surrogate_search                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The improved program adopts a strategy of generating multiple candidate paths using a     │
│                          │ Gaussian potential field and selecting the best one based on a more rigorous surrogate    │
│                          │ scoring method.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **High-Fidelity Scoring**: Instead of evaluating metrics only at vertices, it uses a   │
│                          │ three-point quadrature (sampling at 1/4, 1/2, and 3/4 of each segment). This better       │
│                          │ approximates the continuous integrals of school noise (F2) and signal loss (F3), catching │
│                          │ cases where a segment might graze a penalty zone between nodes.                           │
│                          │ 2. **Deterministic Grid Search**: It searches over a grid of parameters for the Gaussian  │
│                          │ repulsion (school_amp, school_sigma) and attraction (base_pull, base_sigma). This allows  │
│                          │ the path to adapt to different geometric configurations of start, end, school, and base.  │
│                          │ 3. **Optimized Potential Field**: The path is constructed as a baseline straight line     │
│                          │ modified by a repulsion offset from the school and an attraction pull towards the base    │
│                          │ station's Y-coordinate, weighted by distance-based Gaussian kernels.                      │
│                          │ 4. **Enhanced Laplacian Smoothing**: Two passes of alpha-smoothing are applied to the     │
│                          │ final result to minimize the distance penalty (F1) and ensure a natural, flyable          │
│                          │ trajectory.                                                                               │
