│ patch_name               │ exact_gaussian_targeting                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The previous heuristic applied two independent Gaussians (one repelling from the school,  │
│                          │ one attracting to the base). Due to superposition, the exact safe offsets at `(sx, sy)`   │
│                          │ and `(bx, by)` were distorted by the tails of the other Gaussian, sometimes creating a    │
│                          │ "double-dip" that needlessly increased the curve length (worsening F1) or missing the     │
│                          │ target depth (worsening F2/F3).                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To guarantee optimal positioning at exactly `x = sx` (safely away from the school) and `x │
│                          │ = bx` (right at the base) while maintaining single-valley mathematical smoothness to      │
│                          │ drastically improve F1, we introduce an exact 2-Point Gaussian Interpolator. By           │
│                          │ establishing the precise target coordinates for the school-avoidance peak and the         │
│                          │ base-attraction valley, we can analytically solve the 2x2 linear system for the optimal   │
│                          │ Gaussian amplitudes `A_s` and `A_b`. This guarantees the final superposed curve           │
│                          │ intersects exactly the strategic waypoints while minimizing excess distance. It           │
│                          │ effectively shapes the path as a smooth envelope curving precisely away from the school   │
│                          │ and wrapping gently into the base.                                                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
